      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5100 mg/day. The maximum daily dose is generally 2550 mg/day for immediate-release tablets and 2000 mg/day for extended-release. The order is about twice the maximum, which carries a risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity. Its 1700 mg single dose is also above the usual per-dose limit for immediate-release tablets.\n\nPlease confirm the intended regimen. For example:\n- **850 mg PO TID with meals** (2550 mg/day, the usual maximum for IR)\n- **500 mg PO TID with meals** (1500 mg/day)\n- **1000 mg PO BID with meals** (2000 mg/day)\n\nOr tell me if the 1700 mg TID dose was intentional and why. It would also help to know the formulation (IR or ER) and the indication. If you confirm a corrected dose, I'll enter it."
      }
